// "[Permanent] explores" [CR#701.44a]: the rules instruct the permanent
// itself, so a card hands the action to it (`act(target(creature), explore)`)
// and the wrapper records that permanent; written with no such handoff, the
// source permanent explores. Inside the handoff `actor` is the permanent, and
// "that permanent's controller" does every step, so the body hands them on to
// `controllerOf(actor)`, inside which `actor` is that player: they reveal the
// top card of their library; if it is a land card they put it into their hand,
// otherwise they put a +1/+1 counter on "that permanent", the exploring one,
// still in view, and may put the card into their graveyard. The card is read
// back off the library slice the reveal opened, as the printed reminder text
// reads it ("that card"); the hand it goes to is its own owner's, derived
// rather than written [CR#400.3].
KeywordAction(
    name: "explore",
    params: [],
    spelling: "explore",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "explore",
        frame_set: Custom(frames: [[], [ObjectNounPhrase]]),
    ),
    body: act(
        controllerOf(actor),
        sequentially([
            reveal(librarySlice(Top, 1, actor)),
            doIf(
                matches(that(Card), land),
                move(that(Card), wherever, hand),
                sequentially([
                    putCounters(1, p1p1Counter, that(Permanent)),
                    may(move(that(Card), wherever, graveyard)),
                ]),
            ),
        ]),
    ),
)
